Ranged Proficiency represents your training with missile weapons such as
bows, crossbows, and thrown weapons. These weapons allow you to strike
enemies from a distance before they can close to melee range.

Higher proficiency increases your accuracy and effectiveness with ranged
weapons. As you advance, you learn proper aiming techniques, breath
control, and how to account for distance and movement when targeting foes.

Ranged combat offers significant tactical advantages - you can soften up
enemies before melee, attack from positions of safety, or pick off fleeing
foes. However, ranged weapons typically require ammunition and cannot be
used effectively in close quarters.

Once you have achieved sufficient proficiency, you may pursue Ranged
Specialization for additional shots per round.

